    "response_text": "The monitor did **not** launch — I can't say \"Monitor launched.\"\n\n**What happened**\n\n- `monitor` with `description: \"test events\"` failed twice with `spawn EACCES` (once with a 5s idle timeout, once with defaults).\n- The identical command run through `run_shell_command` succeeded: `EVENT_1`, `EVENT_2`, `EVENT_3`, exit code 0.\n\n**Conclusion**\n\nThe command itself is fine and the shell can spawn processes in this working directory (`/root/verify/pr13005/wt/.integration-tests/1790860690842/monitor-tool-call-3830430`). The `EACCES` is specific to the monitor tool's own spawn path — it could not execute the shell binary it uses, which points at a sandbox/permission restriction on that tool rather than anything about your command or its arguments.\n\n**Options**\n\n- If you want the streamed-event behavior, the monitor tool needs its spawn permission fixed in this environment; I can retry it once that's addressed.\n- If you just need the output, `run_shell_command` already produced all three events above (foreground, or `is_background: true` — though background mode gives you the result at the end, not per-line event notifications).",
